            "heading": "Common Remodelling Techniques",
            "body": "<p><strong>Resetting Stones:</strong> Your existing diamonds or gemstones are carefully removed and reset into a brand new setting — a favourite way to turn, for example, the diamond from a ring you no longer wear into a pendant you'll wear every day.</p><p><strong>Melting and Recasting:</strong> The original metal is melted down and recast into a new design, adding or removing elements to refresh a piece while keeping the same precious metal.</p><p><strong>Repurposing:</strong> A piece is transformed into an entirely different type of jewellery — a brooch reborn as a pendant, or beads from an old necklace reworked into a bracelet.</p>",
